tools/pine_survey/cache/

# Per-chunk logs from tools/pytest_chunks.py (the R7 full-lane runner). One
# full run is ~40 MB across 12 logs and is evidence for ONE run, not an
# artifact. Cite a chunk log by path in a commit message; never commit it.
.pytest_chunks/

# ⛔ WORKTREE OWNERSHIP (CLAUDE.md, owner ruling 2026-09-12). Every worktree
# carries one at its root naming the session that created it, so a cleanup can
# tell what it is about to delete. Per-worktree and never committed.
.uct-session-owner

# ⛔ The Pine rig sandbox. `boot_rig.py` REFUSES to resolve here (see
# tests/test_rig_sandbox_never_inside_a_worktree.py) — this entry is the second
# layer, so a hand-run or an older copy of the script cannot dirty the tree either.
rig-data/

# item-4 audit output (screenshots + report.json) — regenerated by tools/pane_gesture_audit.py
tools/pane_audit_out/
docs/notebook/wave-q1-probe-results/local-*.json

# Wave Q1 daily window check writes here every morning. Operational, not a
# record: the durable record is the stamped row in wave-q1-RESUME-HERE.md.
# Tracking it would leave the worktree permanently dirty and every future
# pre-flight would have to explain away a modified file.
docs/notebook/window-check.log

# Gate wrapper shard logs — large, per-run, and regenerated every time. The MANIFESTS
# (.json/.md) beside them are the evidence and stay tracked.
docs/plans/joystick/gate-runs/*.log
# the Notebook's own gate runs: keep the REPORT, never the multi-MB shard logs
docs/notebook/gate-runs/*.log
# nb_gate.py regenerates this beside itself on every run; the LOG is the record
tools/wave-q1-gate-verdict.md
docs/plans/joystick/gate-runs/INVALID-*.md

# RTH scheduled-run logs - per-run, regenerated, and potentially large. The RESULTS
# live in docs/runbooks/monday-rth-results/ and are committed; the transcript does not.
/logs/

# ⛔ B4 mutation-harness sandbox marker. A mutation harness refuses to run unless the tree
# it is about to edit carries this file (see docs/discord-render/instruments/harness_guard.py).
# It is ignored ON PURPOSE and that is the whole argument for a marker over a name pattern:
# no pull, merge, rebase, `git worktree add` or `git checkout` can ever put it in the
# integrator's tree. Somebody has to stand in a throwaway worktree and write it.
.mutation-sandbox

# Breadth Data Charts screenshot harness working output (DC-2 §3.2).
# ⛔ The GOLDENS are tracked (docs/breadth-data-charts/shots-golden/); this is the
# scratch directory a run writes before it is compared, and committing it would
# make every capture a diff.
docs/breadth-data-charts/shots/

# harness run output (regenerated on each run)
tools/intraday_tail_harness_out.json
tools/intraday_scan_out.json

# ⭐ `api/data/naaim_history.csv` IS VERSION-CONTROLLED, for the same reason the
# canonical address book above is: it is DERIVED (tools/build_naaim_seed.py, from
# NAAIM's own public embeddable table) but it is not scratch output. The web pod
# seeds the canonical NAAIM series from it at boot, so a checkout without it starts
# with no history — and a generated file nobody can diff in review is a second
# authority with extra steps.
#
# ⚠️ IT IS TRACKED BY `git add -f`, NOT BY A NEGATION HERE. Git cannot re-include a
# file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded, and line 11's `data/` excludes
# `api/data/`. Every committed file under there — `breadth_sentiment_history.csv`,
# `cap_universe.json`, the voice KB — is tracked the same way. A `!api/data/...`
# line would look like it worked and would not.
tools/intraday_current_out.json
